  "chunks": [
    {
      "chunk_type": "isnad",
      "arabic_text": "مُحَمَّدُ بْنُ يَحْيَى عَنْ مُحَمَّدِ بْنِ أَحْمَدَ عَنِ السِّنْدِيِّ بْنِ مُحَمَّدٍ عَنْ صَفْوَانَ الْجَمَّالِ عَنْ أَبِي عَبْدِ اللَّهِ ( عليه السلام ) قَالَ",
      "translations": {
        "en": "Muhammad ibn Yahya, from Muhammad ibn Ahmad, from Al-Sindi ibn Muhammad, from Safwan al-Jammal, from Abu Abdillah (peace be upon him), who said:"
      }
    },
    {
      "chunk_type": "body",
      "arabic_text": "قُلْتُ لَهُ بِأَبِي أَنْتَ وَ أُمِّي إِنِّي جَعَلْتُ عَلَى نَفْسِي مَشْياً إِلَى بَيْتِ اللَّهِ قَالَ كَفِّرْ يَمِينَكَ فَإِنَّمَا جَعَلْتَ عَلَى نَفْسِكَ يَمِيناً وَ مَا جَعَلْتَهُ لِلَّهِ فَفِ بِهِ",
      "translations": {
        "en": "I said to him, 'May my father and mother be sacrificed for you, I have made it upon myself to walk to the House of Allah.' He said, 'Expiate your oath, for you have made an oath upon yourself, and whatever you made it for the sake of Allah, fulfill it.'"
      }
    }
  ],
  "translations": {
    "en": {
      "summary": "The Imam (peace be upon him) clarifies the legal distinction between a vow (nadhr) and an oath (yamin) regarding walking to the Kaaba. He instructs that since the person made an oath upon themselves to perform the action, they must fulfill the oath by performing the act, but they are required to pay the expiation (kaffarah) for the oath.",
      "seo_question": "What is the ruling on fulfilling an oath to walk to the Kaaba?",
      "key_terms": {
        "مَشْياً": "Walking (on foot)",
        "بَيْتِ اللَّهِ": "The House of Allah (Kaaba)",
        "يَمِينَكَ": "Your oath",
        "كَفْ (oath/vow specifically sworn upon oneself)"
